From 246c1629481117413fd4648cdfc25f6fb24a5502 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: StanleyYP Wang <StanleyYP.Wang@mediatek.com>
Date: Mon, 20 Feb 2023 14:55:49 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 10/28] hostapd: mtk: Add DFS detection mode

Add DFS detection modes to test the radar detection rate. In a detect
mode, the chain that saw the radar stays on its channel: mode 1 holds
the AP channel, mode 2 the background chain, mode 3 both. The mode
applies after hostapd knows which chain saw the radar, so the other
chain acts on its radar as usual. In mode 2, a radar on the AP channel
still moves the AP. A held chain keeps its channel available in the
hostapd channel table, because the kernel sends no end of the
non-occupancy period for a channel it did not mark.

The kernel keeps a DFS state of its own and refuses every beacon
update on a channel it marked unavailable, so hostapd writes the mode
to the detect mode test file of cfg80211 in debugfs as well. The
write happens at the DFS_DETECT_MODE command and at each start of an
interface that runs DFS, with the configured value. Such an interface
writes zero when it stops, so a restart does not leave a stale mode.
A kernel without the file is accepted, and a failed write fails the
command. The configuration file and the command refuse a value that
is not a whole number from 0 to 3, and the previous mode stays.

Signed-off-by: StanleyYP Wang <StanleyYP.Wang@mediatek.com>
Co-developed-by: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
Signed-off-by: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
